<!--
  Device geometry: one shape per input, keyed by PadLayout button id.

  Traced from the device artwork and exported from GIMP, then converted - SVG and
  WPF agree on the M/L/C/Z path commands, so these are the artist's curves rather
  than an approximation of them. Coordinates are in the artwork's own 896x1200
  space; the view scales the whole thing, so nothing here needs to change when the
  window is resized.

  Regenerated wholesale from Paths_Final.svg by scratchpad/togeometry.py. Edit the
  drawing and re-run it; do not hand-edit the shapes below, because the next export
  would silently discard the correction.

  The three LED_* shapes are not controls. They take no clicks and carry no binding:
  they mirror the pad's own indicator lamps for the current mode, so that the picture
  on screen agrees with the hardware in the user's hand.
-->
