  <!--
    Click targets for the eight D-Pad directions.

    The arrows above are what you see; these are what you hit. Traced at their drawn size
    the arrows are pointed and taper to nothing at the tip, so no amount of stroke width
    makes them comfortable to click. The catchment is therefore separated from the drawing:
    BuildShapes uses Geo_Hit_* for the invisible shape that receives the click and the
    traced arrow for the outline it draws, which keeps the artwork intact while making the
    target forgiving.

    Eight 45 degree wedges about the pad center, measured from the traced arrows themselves
    rather than typed in, so redrawing the pad moves these with it. They tile the disc
    exactly: no gaps, so any click inside the pad resolves to a direction, and no overlap,
    so none can steal a neighbor's clicks. The small hole at the center keeps eight sharp
    points from converging on one ambiguous pixel.
  -->
